<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/consumer">Consumer Electronics</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">SMT &amp; Sensor Assembly</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Consumer Electronics products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s active" href="/markets/consumer/smt-sensors"><span class="abbr">SS</span><span class="label">SMT &amp; Sensor Assembly</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/consumer/wireless-charging"><span class="abbr">WC</span><span class="label">Wireless Charging</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the device does and the volumes you expect and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Consumer Electronics &middot; SMT &amp; Sensor Assembly</div><h1 class="mk-h1">SMT and sensor assembly for consumer electronics</h1><p class="mk-lede">Hana supports high-density consumer PCBAs using components including 01005 passives and micro-BGA or WLCSP packages down to 0.2 mm pitch. Placement accuracy reaches ±18 µm on panels up to 440 × 600 mm, with vacuum reflow under nitrogen available where required and inspection integrated throughout the SMT process.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-smt-sensors" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ SMT &amp; Sensor Assembly &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-smt-sensors" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Consumer SMT programs draw on the same microelectronics assembly processes used across Hana's sensor and IC manufacturing operations.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Fine-pitch consumer PCBAs</span></div><div class="desc">High-volume SMT assembly using 01005 passives and micro-BGA or WLCSP packages down to 0.2 mm pitch, with placement accuracy to ±18 µm on panels up to 440 × 600 mm.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">Miniaturized sensor assemblies</span></div><div class="desc">Assembly of sensor die and packaged sensors onto or within the PCBA, supported by Hana's broader microelectronics and sensor-assembly capabilities.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Inspection coverage on every board</span></div><div class="desc">Solder paste inspection before placement, automated optical inspection around the reflow process and X-ray inspection for hidden solder joints.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Functional test on the line</span></div><div class="desc">Acoustic, Bluetooth, wireless and GPS functional testing available to program requirements.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Further process detail covering fine-pitch and high-density assembly, panel handling, depanel and marking is available on the SMT Assembly capability page.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/pcba-box-build/smt-assembly">Explore SMT Assembly <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Holding fine pitch across a long run</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Fine-pitch SMT depends on maintaining control throughout the placement and reflow process. Solder paste inspection measures deposition before placement, while component placement is controlled to ±18 µm. Reflow profiles are developed around the board and component requirements, with vacuum reflow under nitrogen available where reduced voiding is required for bottom-terminated or micro-BGA packages. AOI and X-ray inspection provide additional coverage for visible and hidden solder joints, allowing process variation to be identified during production.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/koh-kong"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Cambodia</span></span><div class="nm">Koh Kong</div><div class="note">high-volume SMT and final assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">SMT and sensor assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">SMT and PCBA</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What consumer products can Hana assemble for?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Compact, dense consumer hardware — wearables, Bluetooth audio, smart-home hubs, remote controls, chargers and connected home devices — supplied as bare PCBAs or as complete, tested units. We do not name the brands we build for.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How does Hana hold quality at consumer volumes?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Inspection is integrated into the production flow. Solder paste inspection runs before placement, automated optical inspection covers the reflow process, and X-ray is used for hidden joints. Functional testing is added where required by the program.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">How small can Hana place and package?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">The fine-pitch envelope runs to 01005 passives and micro-BGA and WLCSP packages at 0.2 mm pitch, placed to ±18 µm, on panels up to 440 × 600 mm. What a given program uses is confirmed with our team against the board.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/consumer" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Consumer Electronics market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your consumer SMT program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>